<!--
  Sophisticated Core compatibility for Minecraft 1.21.11 / NeoForge 21.11.

  1.21.11 moved the mod to the NeoForge transfer API: InventoryHandler extends ItemStacksResourceHandler, the slot
  limit of a normal slot is derived from the item's maximum stack size and the stack upgrade multiplier is expressed
  relative to the vanilla base slot limit of 64, cancelling out again in InventoryHandler#getBaseCapacity. The 1.20.1
  file replaced exactly those 64 constants with the configured maximum stack size; doing that on 1.21.11 would
  multiply the already raised item stack size a second time and is therefore wrong. The corresponding entries were
  dropped:

  - InventoryHandler#getBaseStackLimit / #setBaseSlotLimit: getBaseStackLimit no longer exists, setBaseSlotLimit now
    stores a 64 based multiplier (see InventoryHandlerMixin, which handles the remaining empty-resource capacity).
  - StackUpgradeItem#*: the 64.0 constants are the base the InventoryHandler divides by again, they must stay 64
    (StackUpgradeItemMixin only clamps the result).
  - InventoryHelper#getAnalogOutputSignal: the former lambda is now a normal method and uses a 64.0F *float*
    constant, which replace64D never matched; the formula is self consistent with the 64 based slot limit.
  - CookingLogic#canSmelt: the hardcoded vanilla limit is 99 in 1.21.11, not 64, so it cannot be expressed with
    replace64/replace64D; it is handled by CookingLogicMixin instead.
  - NoopStorageWrapper#getInventoryHandler: the 64 moved into a lambda and must stay 64 based as well.

  What is left are the places where 64 is still the plain vanilla maximum stack size:
  - the client side quick craft preview uses 64 for an empty slot, and
  - StorageContainerMenuBase#mergeItemStack checks whether a slot accepts stacks above the vanilla maximum.
-->
<transformers>
    <class path="net.p3pp3rf1y.sophisticatedcore.client.gui.StorageScreenBase" transformChildren="false">
        <method name="renderSlot" transformer="replace64"
                desc="(Lnet/minecraft/client/gui/GuiGraphics;Lnet/minecraft/world/inventory/Slot;II)V"/>
    </class>

    <class path="net.p3pp3rf1y.sophisticatedcore.common.gui.StorageContainerMenuBase" transformChildren="false">
        <method name="mergeItemStack" transformer="replace64"
                desc="(Lnet/minecraft/world/item/ItemStack;IIZZZ)Lnet/minecraft/world/item/ItemStack;"/>
    </class>
</transformers>
